1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,552
Chapter eighteen — playbooks.

2
00:00:03,612 --> 00:00:10,658
A step on a diagram tells you
nothing about how to run it.

3
00:00:10,718 --> 00:00:15,959
Two experts fix that.

4
00:00:16,019 --> 00:00:25,466
Expand with expert takes a macro step
and breaks it into the real ones.

5
00:00:25,526 --> 00:00:42,672
And Generate playbook makes
this step actually runnable.

6
00:00:42,732 --> 00:01:11,242
A process-operations expert reads the
step, its lane, its inputs and its yield —

7
00:01:11,302 --> 00:01:22,257
— and writes the entry criteria, the sequence,
the checks and the artifacts it produces.

8
00:01:22,317 --> 00:01:33,087
It lands on the step itself, under Playbook.

9
00:01:33,147 --> 00:01:42,095
A playbook a team could
pick up and run tomorrow.

10
00:01:42,155 --> 00:01:50,107
It is kept on the step, and
it exports with the process.

11
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:56,114
Perry the process analyst is one
of six experts on this side —

12
00:01:56,174 --> 00:02:04,181
change management, agile delivery, incidents,
onboarding and procurement are the others.
